cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these study notes, please cite them using the metadata below."
title: "Study Notes on Reinforcement Learning: An Introduction (2nd Ed.)"
abstract: >-
  Independent personal study notes accompanying Richard S. Sutton and Andrew G.
  Barto's Reinforcement Learning: An Introduction (2nd ed., MIT Press, 2018; 2020 corrected reprint).
  Covers all 13 chapters across tabular and approximate solution methods, built
  as a Quarto book (HTML, PDF, EPUB) with an accompanying Anki cloze flashcard
  deck. Intended solely as a study companion and not as a substitute for the
  textbook.
authors:
